 ## Unreleased
 
+### Hardening against five observed failure modes
+
+Five changes, each answering a failure seen in executed runs: a reclassification that shrank the reviewer panel (FM1), runs that died without a report (FM2), a spec amended in the middle of a run (FM3), unbounded spend by one station (FM4), and review launched on incomplete work (FM5).
+
+- Classification floor (FM1): intake proposes risk and surfaces and deterministic rules decide. Intake may raise the risk and add surfaces, never lower or remove what was submitted; a low rating is refused on an unrated work order that carries a scanned risk hint. After the builder, the changed file paths can add surfaces and raise low to medium when an undeclared security, data, payments or deploy surface is touched, and reviewers are routed again before any runs. `routing.json` and `report.md` record the decisions and each escalation. Spec: classification-floor. Doc: docs/ROUTING.md.
+- Run checkpoint (FM2): `report.json` is saved atomically after every station and before every agent call, with `run_state` `in_progress`, `completed` or `aborted`. An interrupted or crashed run keeps its completed steps, names the station in flight and carries the usage that station had reported. `anvil run` turns SIGTERM into an exit the runner records. There is no resume. Spec: run-checkpoint. Doc: docs/RUN-CHECKPOINT.md.
+- Write authority (FM3): the runner hashes the protected files around every executed agent station. A station that modifies or deletes an existing protected file it does not own makes the approver reject the run; the builder also fails the pre-review gate when it amends a test or spec written earlier in the same run. Default protected paths are now `tests/`, `.openspec/`, `anvil.json` and `.anvil/`; spec-writer and blueprint own `.openspec/`, test-writer owns `tests/`. The protected path rule applies even with no checks configured. The report gains an `integrity` section. Spec: write-authority. Docs: docs/WRITE-AUTHORITY.md, docs/CHECKS-GATE.md.
+- Station token caps (FM4): `efficiency.max_station_tokens` (500,000 in new projects) and `efficiency.station_tokens.<station>` cap one station call. The station is handed the smaller of its cap and the remaining run pool; an overrun is marked `station_cap_exceeded` with a report warning. The cap is enforced between attempts, a running call cannot be cut off. Spec: station-token-caps. Doc: docs/COST-MEASUREMENT.md.
+- Checks in new projects (FM5): blueprints may name `checks`; `new-project` writes them and the default protected paths into `anvil.json`, `init` and `onboard` write the protected paths with an empty checks list, and BLUEPRINT.md states the checks. The python-service blueprint runs `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`. Spec: scaffold-checks.
+- This repository's own `anvil.json` now protects `.openspec/` and `.anvil/` as well.
+
+### Six capabilities taken from what other factories do best
+
+- Sealed tests and specs: the runner keeps a copy of every protected file before each station and writes it back when a station changes one without authority, so the checks gate always runs against the tests as written. The violation is still recorded and still fails the attempt. `restore_protected: false` switches it off. Spec: sealed-tests. Doc: docs/WRITE-AUTHORITY.md.
+- Resume: `anvil run --resume` continues an aborted run from its first unfinished station. Finished steps are carried with their usage, the panel and the reviews already written are restored from the run record, and the aborted report is not archived twice. Spec: run-resume. Doc: docs/RUN-CHECKPOINT.md.
+- In-run loopback: with `loopback_mode: in_run` (or `--loopback in-run`) the runner sends failed work back and runs it again inside the same run, bounded by max_loopbacks and the run budget. The returning station receives the findings and the gate output. The default stays `record`. Spec: in-run-loopback. Doc: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md.
+- Pre-build gate: before the builder is called, deterministic code checks that every scenario of the specs the run works from appears in the tests and, when `require_checks` is set, that the project has a check command. A failure ends the run `gate_failed` without paying for the build. Spec: pre-build-gate. Doc: docs/CHECKS-GATE.md.
+- Outcome metrics: first pass approval, approval and loopback rates, gate failure rate, objections per reviewer and tokens per approved work order, computed from the reports on record. Shown on the status page, written to `status/usage.json`, printed by `anvil metrics`. Spec: outcome-metrics. Doc: docs/STATUS-PAGE.md.
+- Clean context reviewer: the new `reviewer-clean` station (station 28) gets the change and nothing else, on a different model family from the builder's. Opt in through the new `sdlc-clean-review` pipeline (pipeline 9); `sdlc-default` is unchanged. Spec: clean-review. Doc: docs/CLEAN-REVIEW.md.
+
