 <section id="problem" class="band"><div class="wrap split"><div><div class="label">The problem</div><h2>A convincing demo<br>isn't a review.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">When the agent that writes the code also tests and approves it, confidence becomes a closed loop.</p><p>And when a demo leaves no spec, test evidence or run record, nobody can audit what happened. ANVIL separates the work from its judgment and keeps the artifacts in your repository.</p></div></div></section>
 <section id="how-it-works" class="band"><div class="wrap"><div class="label">How it works</div><h2>A factory line.<br>Not a longer prompt.</h2><p class="lead">The spec comes before implementation. Tests come before the build.</p><p>Each station has a contract and an assigned artifact. Pipelines compose those stations into a line that fits the work: software, content, a new project or an existing codebase.</p>
